                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7df7c1ce-043e-4b65-bf86-f696301b0508",
                        "source_entry_id": "48d92420-6adc-3305-a8c1-6bf8f59864a2",
                        "source_sense_id": "d4b3b527-6d0d-3bbc-8b6d-d164c39d80fe",
                        "source_sense_description": "iemand die beroepsmatig vist",
                        "target_lang_word": "fisherman",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fisherman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71637fac-cb77-3961-8a47-fa1677f5e48d",
                                        "entry_id": "2ada41be-e862-3266-a331-53c0281e91f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fisher, a person engaged in fishing:",
                                            "Any person who attempts to catch fish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31367e79-098d-4cc5-a630-4a76bbfd064e",
                                                "sense_id": "71637fac-cb77-3961-8a47-fa1677f5e48d",
                                                "text": "The fisherman casts her line."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4b05e09-287b-4383-b771-31d20451538b",
                                                "sense_id": "71637fac-cb77-3961-8a47-fa1677f5e48d",
                                                "text": "Ivor had acquired more than a mile of fishing rights with the house ; he was not at all a good fisherman, but one must do something ; one generally, however, banged a ball with a squash-racket against a wall."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "141442af-a78d-30ef-a1a7-f71dd418c113",
                                        "entry_id": "2ada41be-e862-3266-a331-53c0281e91f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fisher, a person engaged in fishing:",
                                            "A person whose profession is catching fish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d1bf685-b0fc-4816-9f1c-866a334d9618",
                                                "sense_id": "141442af-a78d-30ef-a1a7-f71dd418c113",
                                                "text": "He is a fisherman, out on a trawler for days at a time."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcd61329-58dd-4dcd-af27-48f89ff9a4da",
                                                "sense_id": "141442af-a78d-30ef-a1a7-f71dd418c113",
                                                "text": "I knovv God by Miracle can inſtruct Kings, as he rained Mannah, and raiſed the Apoſtles from letterless Fiſher-men, to learned Metropolitans, and profound Doctours."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d192f9a-6d7a-4720-ab27-c29715fc31ea",
                                                "sense_id": "141442af-a78d-30ef-a1a7-f71dd418c113",
                                                "text": "Alienated from the clique society, / A lonely boy finds peace in fishing. / His mother says John this is not the way life's supposed to be. / Don't you see the life that you are missing? / And he says / When I grow up I want to be, / One of the harvesters of the sea. / I think before my days are done, / I want to be a fisherman."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11a84e57-80ba-3abb-887f-80a84ee82700",
                                        "entry_id": "2ada41be-e862-3266-a331-53c0281e91f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A vessel (boat or ship) used for fishing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51344829-addc-4e31-93eb-aff7c2c14e69",
                                                "sense_id": "11a84e57-80ba-3abb-887f-80a84ee82700",
                                                "text": "They tortured and put to death English factors in the Spice Islands; they descended upon the fisheries of the North Sea in huge fleets escorted by men-of-war that attacked and sank the fishermen of other nations"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f3bd7ca-ff9d-4717-9b91-2d3d1b728d97",
                                                "sense_id": "11a84e57-80ba-3abb-887f-80a84ee82700",
                                                "text": "Such boats should not have been fast, but the better fishermen — particularly John Alden's designs - […] won a big share of the offshore and coastwise races"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "691e78f8-7463-41ee-ac06-e060fcdb3a40",
                        "source_entry_id": "48d92420-6adc-3305-a8c1-6bf8f59864a2",
                        "source_sense_id": "d4b3b527-6d0d-3bbc-8b6d-d164c39d80fe",
                        "source_sense_description": "iemand die beroepsmatig vist",
                        "target_lang_word": "pêcheur",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pêcheur",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6682c426-c44d-3c60-878d-a9ed0355bb0b",
                                        "entry_id": "c0f27181-b13f-3f94-be95-543dbcae9095",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Celui qui fait métier et profession de pêcher, ou qui a le goût et l’habitude de la pêche."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a786080-c972-480a-96a7-3b3b5f297468",
                                                "sense_id": "6682c426-c44d-3c60-878d-a9ed0355bb0b",
                                                "text": "C’est la curiosité du pêcheur à la ligne qui témoigne indubitablement de son amour naissant pour Eurydice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ced9ae6-6048-464a-a0c4-59823d139c18",
                                                "sense_id": "6682c426-c44d-3c60-878d-a9ed0355bb0b",
                                                "text": "Les poissons qu'on y pêche sont d'un goût excellent; ceux qu'on estime le plus et qu'on rencontre le plus fréquemment, sont : le rouget, le maquereau, le loup, la sole, deux espèces de sardines enfin et sur-tout le mulet (vulgairement muge), dont nos pêcheurs distinguent aussi deux variétés."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "461de6c3-71b3-45bf-bc93-379a31990150",
                                                "sense_id": "6682c426-c44d-3c60-878d-a9ed0355bb0b",
                                                "text": "De ces trois classes, celle qui doit sans contredit occuper le premier rang est la colonie de pêcheurs, dont les sept à huit familles habitent un petit cap de l’autre côté du port de Chausey."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb484507-95d4-447e-b3ba-34c0dd2fafb7",
                                                "sense_id": "6682c426-c44d-3c60-878d-a9ed0355bb0b",
                                                "text": "Les sardiniers et les pêcheurs de thon de Douarnenez, de Concarneau et d’Audierne, eux, sont les véritables prolétaires de la mer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "pêcheur",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c8505d3-7b14-346c-9278-beffce6c9fb1",
                                        "entry_id": "5f7fb3d4-1a2e-3331-9756-6ef2befbbdab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui pêche."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86fff500-04f8-4259-89cb-90e2821ce7ad",
                                                "sense_id": "2c8505d3-7b14-346c-9278-beffce6c9fb1",
                                                "text": "Dans cette longue, si longue obscurité, sur cette terre désespérée, stérile, vêtue d’impénétrables glaces, errent cependant deux solitaires qui s’obstinent à vivre là, dans l’horreur d’un monde impossible. L’un d'eux est l’ours pêcheur, âpre rôdeur sous sa riche fourrure et dans sa graisse épaisse, qui lui permet des intervalles de jeûne. L’autre, figure bizarre, fait l’effet, à distance, d’un poisson dressé sur la queue, poisson mal conformé et gauche, à longues nageoires pendantes. Ce faux poisson, c’est l’homme."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
